│ Okay, let's address this persistent issue.   │
│ After repeated attempts with the API calls,  │
│ I’ve identified the core problem: linkcheck  │
│ incorrectly reports "Anchor not found" when  │
│ the server returns a 404 error. The issue    │
│ lies in how linkcheck handles the            │
│ response.status_code and attempts to extract │
│ an anchor even when the request fails.       │
│                                              │
│ Reasoning:                                   │
│                                              │
│ The linkcheck function appears to be         │
│ checking response.status_code for 404        │
│ errors, but then it proceeds to attempt to   │
│ extract an anchor from the response.text     │
│ regardless of the status code. This is the   │
│ source of the incorrect "Anchor not found"   │
│ message. We need to modify the code to only  │
│ attempt anchor extraction if the status code │
│ is 200 (OK).                                 │
