│ Okay, let’s address this. After repeated     │
│ failures with the API calls, I’ve analyzed   │
│ the code context provided and identified the │
│ root cause of the issue. The linkcheck       │
│ function incorrectly reports "Anchor not     │
│ found" when a 404 error is returned. This is │
│ because it doesn't properly handle the HTTP  │
│ status code and continues to attempt anchor  │
│ extraction even when the server indicates a  │
│ failure. The fix involves checking the       │
│ response.status_code and only proceeding     │
│ with anchor extraction if the status code    │
│ indicates success (e.g., 200).               │
