│ Okay, let's address this. After repeated     │
│ failures with the API calls, I’ve analyzed   │
│ the code around response.status_code and     │
│ response.text within the linkcheck function. │
│ The issue is that when a 404 error occurs,   │
│ linkcheck incorrectly reports an "Anchor not │
│ found" error instead of the expected HTTP    │
│ error. This is because it’s not properly     │
│ handling the 404 status code and continuing  │
│ to attempt to extract the anchor.            │
│                                              │
│ Reasoning: The core problem is that          │
│ linkcheck doesn't correctly interpret a 404  │
│ status code. It should treat this as a       │
│ failed link and report the appropriate HTTP  │
│ error, rather than assuming the anchor is    │
│ missing. The current logic incorrectly       │
│ assumes the anchor is missing when the       │
│ server returns a 404.                        │
│                                              │
│ Here's the patch:                            │
│                                              │
│ ┏━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━┓ │
